"""Static validation of builder-defined tools for an agent project.

Four authoring checks run at train/validate time:

- :func:`validate_tool_references` — every tool named by a skill (an
  ``@tool.<name>`` prose reference, ``execute_tool`` step, or skill/flow
  ``tools:`` gate) must
  resolve the way the runtime resolves it: skill-local ``@tool`` functions
  (``skills/<skill_id>/tools.py`` and ``skills/<skill_id>/tools/*.py``), the
  shared agent-root ``tools/*.py`` functions the skill *declares* via its
  gates, or a declared MCP import. Python tools are loaded the same way the
  runtime loads them (import-based), so a missing file, an import error, or a
  name mismatch all surface here. MCP tool existence is checked when the
  runtime connects to the remote server.
- :func:`validate_tool_memory_writes` — a static AST scan of every tool module
  for ``<param>.memory.set("<literal>", ...)`` calls, checking each literal
  entry name resolves to a declared memory entry. Skill-local modules check
  against the owning skill's schema plus the project schema; shared modules
  check against the union of all skills' schemas plus the project schema
  (a shared tool runs in a declaring skill's context, so per-skill precision
  stays on the runtime backstop). This mirrors the runtime backstop
  (:meth:`~rasa.mantle.memory.manager.MemoryManager.set`), which rejects
  undeclared writes — but catches them before a conversation hits the write.
  Non-literal (dynamically computed) entry names cannot be checked statically
  and stay on the runtime backstop.
- :func:`validate_tool_memory_bypass` — a static AST scan of the same tool
  modules for ``.memory._memory``, ``getattr(..., "_memory")``,
  ``attrgetter("_memory")``, and ``.clear_entries(...)``. Those reach the
  conversation-wide memory manager and can write another skill. Public
  ``context.memory.set`` on this skill (or project) is the supported write path.
  Imported helpers in non-tool modules are not scanned; this is authoring lint,
  not a runtime sandbox.
- :func:`validate_button_source_tools` — every ``buttons.source`` on a
  skill-local or project ``responses.yml`` variant must name a local,
  non-confirming ``@tool``. MCP imports and confirmation-gated tools are
  rejected. A project-root source must be referenced by at least one skill
  that can observe that response.

Each check returns :class:`~rasa.mantle.validation_finding.ValidationFinding`
objects so :func:`rasa.mantle.validation.validate_project` can aggregate them.
"""

